It sounds to me as if you are not advancing your equipment to match
your level so you get nasties that you can't handle.

My answer to this in vanilla is to use a class that gains abilities
very quickly as they level up so they don't need to struggle so much
with gear.

The classes I suggest you try are:

Wizard: Rapid gain of spell points and no loss of food with casting.

Monk: Unarmed skill advances quickly and can punch their way out of a
paper golem blockade.

Rogue: Grab a mirror from a nymph and use ordinary daggers in
combination with the mirror for an attack that gets nastier than the
nasties advance.  (Wishing for Magicbane at exp level 4 can't hurt...)

